    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0512" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg398"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d179-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-25">25 July 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Former Naval Person to President. Personal and most secret. Number 379.</p>
                <p>My immediately preceding telegram. Me. Beware of spurious imitations <hi
                        rendition="#italic">vide</hi> mission to Moscow.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d179-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d179-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d179-f1-content">
                <p>Channel of transmission not indicated.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d179-f2" n="2" xml:id="d179-f2-content">
                <p>The reference is presumably to the motion picture, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mission to Moscow</hi>, in which the role of Churchill was portrayed by
                    Dudley Field Malone, who had served as Third Assistant Secretary of State under
                    President Wilson at a time when Roosevelt was Assistant Secretary of the
                    Navy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
